+ * pool of the first mbuf in the chain.  When a chain spans multiple pools,
+ * this could cause the destination segment to be smaller than the source
+ * segment, leading to payload overruns.
+ *
+ * This revised version allocates each duplicated segment from the same pool
+ * as the corresponding source segment (`om->om_omp`).  This preserves the
+ * capacity, contents and ensures no writes beyond the destination payload
+ * area.
+ */
